# Copy to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev`, or export as env vars for the Node server.
# All of these are OPTIONAL. GhostTrace is fully functional without any of them —
# every core source is free and keyless.

# https://account.shodan.io/  -> service banners, product names and versions per
# open port, beyond the free InternetDB's port list.
SHODAN_API_KEY=

# https://www.virustotal.com/gui/my-apikey  -> reputation scoring for domains and IPs,
# including which specific vendors flagged them.
VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY=

# https://www.abuseipdb.com/account/api  -> abuse confidence score, usage type, and
# the report categories that explain what an address was actually reported for.
ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY=

# https://viz.greynoise.io/account/  -> distinguishes internet-wide background
# scanning from traffic aimed at you specifically, which is the difference between
# an alert worth reading and one worth ignoring.
GREYNOISE_API_KEY=

# https://console.twilio.com/  -> CNAM caller-ID name and post-portability carrier
# for phone lookups. This is the ONLY source here that can return a subscriber or
# business name, and it is billed per lookup (roughly $0.01). US coverage for
# caller name; line-type intelligence is international.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/  -> runs the search a human would run
# for a phone number and returns the actual titles and snippets, instead of just
# building dork links. The highest-yield technique for naming a business number.
# Free tier: 2,000 queries/month, 1 query/second.
#
# There is no keyless alternative that works from a Worker: DuckDuckGo's HTML
# endpoint returns a bot challenge to datacenter addresses, its Instant Answer
# API has nothing for phone numbers, and public SearxNG instances serve a
# captcha. All three were tested.
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# https://haveibeenpwned.com/API/Key  -> breach exposure for an email address:
# which breaches, when, and what data class was exposed in each. HIBP is the only
# authoritative source for this and the key is paid (~$4/month). Without it, the
# email lookup says nothing about breach exposure rather than guessing.
HIBP_API_KEY=

# https://github.com/settings/tokens  -> a classic token with NO scopes is enough;
# this is purely for rate limiting, not access.
#
# Worth setting even though nothing depends on it. Unauthenticated GitHub API
# requests are capped at 60/hour and search at 10/minute PER SOURCE ADDRESS, and
# on shared egress — a Worker, a VPN, a datacenter — that budget is routinely
# already spent by unrelated traffic. Without a token, an empty GitHub result in
# an email or username lookup is not evidence of anything.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
